# Copy this file to functions/.env to configure the Cloud Functions
# deployment. Firebase deploys functions/.env automatically alongside the
# code, so anything here becomes process.env at runtime.
#
# Never commit the real .env file.

# ── Firebase App Check enforcement ───────────────────────────────────
# When 'true', every callable in this backend rejects requests that don't
# carry a valid App Check token, before the handler runs. That is what
# stops a script from replaying the app's public Firebase config against
# these functions.
#
# Leave unset (or 'false') until the web app is actually sending tokens,
# or you will lock out every real user. The order that works:
#
#   1. Register a reCAPTCHA v3 site key (Google reCAPTCHA admin console)
#      and add it to Firebase Console → App Check for this web app.
#   2. Put that key in the web app's .env as VITE_RECAPTCHA_V3_SITE_KEY
#      and deploy the frontend. See src/services/firebase.js.
#   3. Watch Firebase Console → App Check until verified requests are the
#      overwhelming majority. Each function also logs
#      appCheck: verified|absent (see shared/withCallable.ts), so the
#      Functions logs answer the same question.
#   4. Only then set this to true and redeploy functions.
#
# Rolling back is just setting this to false and redeploying.
APPCHECK_ENFORCED=false
